cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ldraw-mcp in your work, please cite it as below."
title: ldraw-mcp
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that renders LDraw models
  (.ldr / .mpd / .dat) to images using real part geometry — studs, slopes,
  transparent glass, rubber tires — via headless Blender and the ImportLDraw
  addon. It gives vision-capable language models an accurate view of a brick
  build, so that export faults a geometric proxy render would hide (crossed
  rotation matrices, floating plates, sunken windows) become visible.
type: software
